  "step_2": "The individual states: 'Fast die selbe Wahrscheinlichkeit, daher habe ich mich für den höheren Gewinn entschieden.' This translates to: 'The probabilities are almost the same, so I chose the higher prize.' The individual notes that the probabilities are similar and bases the decision on selecting the lottery with the higher guaranteed payout (2500 Euros vs. 2400 Euros). The deliberation process focuses on the magnitude of the positive outcome, not on the distribution of probabilities or skewness. There is no mention of risk, probability distribution, unfavorable outcomes, or skewness in the reasoning. The justification is based solely on the higher expected value (or simply the higher prize), not on skewness or asymmetry in the probability distribution.",
